{"id":"CVE-2010-5106","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2012-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-17T03:17:40.692Z","description":"The XML-RPC remote publishing interface in xmlrpc.php in WordPress before 3.0.3 does not properly check capabilities, which allows remote authenticated users to bypass intended access restrictions, and publish, edit, or delete posts, by leveraging the Author or Contributor role.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://codex.wordpress.org/Version_3.0.3","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2012/09/14/10","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20120914 Re: CVE-request: WordPress insufficient permissions verification on XMLRPC interface"},{"url":"http://core.trac.wordpress.org/changeset/16803","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["wordpress"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-5293","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2014-01-21T01:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T16:23:45.618Z","description":"wp-includes/comment.php in WordPress before 3.0.2 does not properly whitelist trackbacks and pingbacks in the blogroll, which allows remote attackers to bypass intended spam restrictions via a crafted URL, as demonstrated by a URL that triggers a substring match.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/13887","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/changeset/16637","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://codex.wordpress.org/Version_3.0.2","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["wordpress"]}
